  "evidenceDistinctions": {
    "initialTransportLoss": "Original gates completed and their hashes/results were read back, but full private files became unavailable when the exec service lost session67365. executor-loss-witness.json preserves the observed facts. The same frozen commands were reissued solely to restore durable raw evidence; recovered receipts use their own actual identities and are not reconstructed historical files.",
    "decimalReceiverCorrection": "The first successor native receipt retains exit1 after two passing groups because the receiver demanded fixed-scale strings2.20/29.80. Actual successful readback is2.2/29.8; corrected independent exact-decimal assertions verify the same values while retaining raw strings. Original proposal price strings remain exact12.30/7.40. No product change.",
    "staticReceiverCorrection": "A static source Merkle helper initially omitted its final return and used the recursive endpoint\u2019s echoed tree-ish instead of canonical commit.tree.sha. Raw failure, original source/input and the corrected complete-tree verification are retained. No product change.",
    "browserFault": "The original six-group receiver forwards the native Worker unchanged and copies actual request/reply data. It injects one declared ErrorEvent on that actual Worker only for the existing unavailable-state control. It substitutes no response, Python code, API or product state. No fault is injected in the successor journey."
